{
  "_description": "Pentium 4 (NetBurst, Northwood 3.0 GHz, 130 nm) single-core wrong-path config, derived from golden_cove.json. No L3 (L2 connects straight to DRAM) and no second-level TLB (DTLB/ITLB miss straight to the page walker). The 12K-uop trace cache is modeled as the DIB; there is no conventional L1I, so the L1I is a tiny streaming buffer in front of the L2. Not modeled: 128-byte sectored L2 lines (block_size stays 64), double-pumped ALUs (folded into execute_width), replay, the FSB/northbridge latency, and the hard-coded BTB (1024x8) / gshare (16K entries) sizes.",
